## Ported extractors (this tree)

### Gofile — `core/udl/extractors/gofile.py`
- Upstream: https://github.com/ltsdw/gofile-downloader
- License: GPL-3.0
- Ported from commit: 48349ba3d017d4531bc3bc3d150e365bdd98f0d6
- Notes: Guest account creation (`POST api.gofile.io/accounts`) and
  `X-Website-Token` generation follow upstream public-link behaviour.
  Token salt may rotate; failures should surface as clear errors.

### Bunkr — `core/udl/extractors/bunkr.py`
- Upstream: https://github.com/Lysagxra/BunkrDownloader
- License: GPL-3.0
- Ported from commit: a58790ff540e8d9b0579c1b1c4d1b49d4fa9b8da
- Notes: Album and single-file resolution, signing API
  (`glb-apisign.cdn.cr/sign`), download API (`dl.bunkr.cr/api/_001_v2`).
  Domains rotate; keep FALLBACK_DOMAIN and URL patterns maintainable.

### Bilibili — `core/udl/extractors/bilibili/`
- Upstream: https://github.com/ScottSloan/Bili23-Downloader
- License: GPL-3.0
- Ported from commit: e3d6aff32fffca88b249412b92b40448321418c4
- Notes: Subset only — BV/av multi-part video, b23.tv short links,
  bangumi/episode when freely accessible. WBI signing, playurl DASH
  selection, and FFmpeg merge patterns adapted from upstream
  (`util/parse/parser/*`, `util/ffmpeg`). Qt worker/thread model was
  not ported. No paywall, VIP-only, or region-lock bypass.
  Upstream README also states a non-commercial usage agreement; GPL
  itself does not forbid commercial use — both are documented here.
  QR/cookie login is stubbed for a later release (OS keychain).

